-- title:
--   Finite étale local algebras over a crossing model are crossing models
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $E$ be a positive natural number. Write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,a$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(a)$, and $\mathrm{const}\,a\,w$ for the class of the constant series $C(w)$. Let $R_0$ be a Noetherian local commutative ring together with a ring isomorphism $e_0 \colon R_0 \simeq \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^E)$, and let $B_1$ be a local commutative $R_0$-algebra which is module-finite over $R_0$, faithful as an $R_0$-module, and étale over $R_0$. The assertion is that there exist a commutative ring $W'$ which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, a ring homomorphism $\sigma' \colon W \to W'$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W'} = (\sigma'\pi)$, and a ring isomorphism $e \colon B_1 \simeq \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W'\,((\sigma'\pi)^E)$ such that: whenever $e_0(r) = \mathrm{const}\,(\pi^E)\,w$ for $r \in R_0$ and $w \in W$, the image of $r$ in $B_1$ satisfies $e(r) = \mathrm{const}\,((\sigma'\pi)^E)\,(\sigma'w)$; every $b \in B_1$ differs from $e^{-1}(\mathrm{const}\,((\sigma'\pi)^E)\,w')$ by an element of $\mathfrak{m}_{B_1}$, for some $w' \in W'$; and $e$ carries the images in $B_1$ of $e_0^{-1}(U(\pi^E))$ and $e_0^{-1}(V(\pi^E))$ to $U((\sigma'\pi)^E)$ and $V((\sigma'\pi)^E)$ respectively. All objects live in the same universe as $W$.
--
--   This is the recognition statement for étale neighbourhoods of a crossing point: a finite étale local algebra over the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ of thickness $E$ is again a crossing model of the same thickness, over an unramified extension $W'$ of the coefficients realising the residue field of the algebra, compatibly with the two branch coordinates and with constants. It is used in the analysis of completed local rings of modular curves at supersingular crossing points, being cited by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isInvariant_of_card_inertia_eq_of_isUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isInvariant_of_card_inertia_eq_of_isUnit).
